@baseUrl = http://localhost:9001

# Office/text document upload (CON-280) for POST /api/content-bank/assets/upload.
# All requests require authentication — run "Login" from sessions/sessions.http first.
# Needs document-service running (default `docker compose up`) and GEMINI_API_KEY
# set (chunks are embedded).
#
# Accepted: .docx/.docm/.dotx, .xlsx/.xlsm/.xltx, .pptx/.pptm/.potx,
# .odt/.ods/.odp (+ flat .fodt/.fods/.fodp), .epub, .csv/.tsv, .html/.xhtml,
# .eml, .rtf, .txt/.log — max 50 MB. Legacy binary / password-protected Office
# files (OLE2) are rejected up front.
#
# The asset lands as type=DOC, status=pending; document-service parses it into
# source-anchored chunks asynchronously → ready / partial / failed. A failed
# asset carries failure_code + failure_reason (CON-312).
#
# Fixtures: sample.docx (headings → section anchors), sample.csv (sheet anchors).

### Upload DOCX  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="Q3 launch plan.docx"
Content-Type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document

< ./sample.docx
--boundary--

> {% client.global.set("docAssetId", response.body.results[0].asset_id) %}

### Get document asset (poll until status=ready|partial|failed)  [protected]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{docAssetId}}
Accept: application/json

### List its chunks with source_label / source_anchor (CON-312)  [protected]
# Expect section anchors from the headings, e.g. source_label "Q3 Launch Plan › Audience".
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{docAssetId}}/chunks?offset=0&limit=50
Accept: application/json

### Rename it — title-only save keeps the anchored chunks (CON-312)  [protected]
# Omitting content (or sending it unchanged) keeps the extracted text.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{docAssetId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Q3 launch plan (final)"
}

### Content edit on an ingested asset (expects 409 code=content_locked)  [protected]
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{docAssetId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Q3 launch plan (final)",
  "content": "hand-edited text"
}

### Upload CSV (sheet anchors)  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="channel-stats.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./sample.csv
--boundary--

> {% client.global.set("csvAssetId", response.body.results[0].asset_id) %}

### List CSV chunks (expect kind=sheet with a cell_range)  [protected]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{csvAssetId}}/chunks
Accept: application/json

### Upload plain text  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="notes.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

Launch checklist: finalize the landing page, schedule the announcement thread,
record the demo video, and brief the two design partners before Tuesday.
--boundary--

### Upload a legacy .doc (expects failed, code=extension_not_allowed)  [protected]
# Legacy binary extensions aren't routed at all. A password-protected .docx (an
# OLE2 container under a .docx name) gets code=unsupported_media_type instead:
# `< ./protected.docx`.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="legacy.doc"
Content-Type: application/msword

not really a doc
--boundary--

### Upload a corrupt .docx (created, then settles failed with code=invalid_file)  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="broken.docx"
Content-Type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document

this is not a zip archive
--boundary--

> {% client.global.set("brokenDocAssetId", response.body.results[0].asset_id) %}

### Get the corrupt document (expect status=failed, failure_code=invalid_file)  [protected]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{brokenDocAssetId}}
Accept: application/json

### Delete the document asset  [protected]
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{docAssetId}}
